---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Tldr from '../../components/Tldr.astro';
import TryItNow from '../../components/TryItNow.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/CopyPrompt.astro';
import KeyTakeaways from '../../components/KeyTakeaways.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="M365 Plugins"
  description="Use Claude inside Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, and Excel — no tab-switching required."
  pageId="m365"
  readMinutes={6}
>
  <PageHeader
    icon="📎"
    title="Claude in Microsoft 365"
    subtitle="You don't always have to go to Claude. Sometimes Claude comes to you."
    readMinutes={6}
  />

  <Tldr>
    <p>
      Claude plugins live <strong>inside Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, and Excel</strong> — the apps
      you're already in all day. No tab-switching, no copy-pasting. Just highlight, click, and get
      the help you need right where the work is happening.
    </p>
  </Tldr>

  <div class="prose-content">
    <p>
      There's a version of Claude that lives on a tab in your browser. Then there's the version
      that shows up inside the app you already have open. The M365 plugins are the latter — a
      Claude sidebar (or right-click menu) embedded directly into the Microsoft tools your day
      already runs on. Less friction, faster results.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Outlook -->
  <section class="mb-10 reveal">
    <h2 class="mb-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">📧 Outlook</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-muted">Your inbox is not a to-do list. Let Claude help you triage it like one.</p>

    <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 mb-5">
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Draft replies in your voice</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Give Claude the context ("I need to push back on this deadline but stay friendly") and it writes the reply. You edit, you send. Done in 30 seconds.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Summarize long threads</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">That 47-message chain from last Tuesday? Ask Claude "what do I actually need to do?" and get the action items without reading the whole saga.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Turn chaos into a crisp follow-up</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Rambling thread, no clear owner, no next steps. Claude synthesizes it into a clean follow-up email ready to send to the whole group.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <CopyPrompt text="Summarize this email thread and tell me: (1) what decisions were made, (2) what I need to do, and (3) if there's anything still unresolved." />
  </section>

  <!-- Word -->
  <section class="mb-10 reveal">
    <h2 class="mb-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">📄 Word</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-muted">Your document, improved — without leaving the document.</p>

    <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 mb-5">
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Summarize & critique in place</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Open a doc, ask Claude for a one-paragraph summary and what's missing. Great for reviewing vendor proposals or policy drafts without reading every word.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Rewrite for a different audience</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Engineering spec that needs to become an exec summary? Highlight the section, ask Claude to rewrite it for a non-technical audience. No separate doc needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">First drafts from outlines</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Paste a bullet outline and ask Claude to expand it into a full section. You get a draft that's 80% there — you bring the last 20% of judgment and nuance.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <CopyPrompt text="I've pasted an outline below. Expand it into a full draft. Use clear, direct language — no buzzwords. Flag anywhere you're uncertain about the details so I can fill them in." />
  </section>

  <!-- PowerPoint -->
  <section class="mb-10 reveal">
    <h2 class="mb-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">📊 PowerPoint</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-muted">Because nobody ever said "I wish I spent more time making slides."</p>

    <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 mb-5">
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Outline a deck from a doc</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Paste a report or brief and ask Claude to propose a slide outline with titles and one-line summaries per slide. Skeleton in seconds, not hours.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Punch up slide headlines</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">"Q3 Results" is a topic, not a headline. Ask Claude to rewrite your titles as declarative statements that tell the story even if someone only reads the headers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Speaker notes from slides</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Paste your slide content and ask Claude to write speaker notes that anticipate audience questions and hit the key talking points — without sounding like a script.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <CopyPrompt text="Here are my slide titles and bullet points. Write speaker notes for each slide — 3–5 sentences, conversational tone, and flag any slide where the content might need more data or a stronger point." />
  </section>

  <!-- Excel -->
  <section class="mb-10 reveal">
    <h2 class="mb-1 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">📈 Excel</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-muted">Formulas are a language. Claude is fluent.</p>

    <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 mb-5">
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Plain-English formula explainer</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Paste any formula — even a nested horror show — and ask Claude to explain it step by step in plain English. Your future self will thank you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Suggest formulas from a description</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">"I want to look up a value in another sheet based on two matching columns." Just describe what you need and Claude returns the formula, ready to paste.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hover-lift rounded-[12px] border border-border bg-card p-4">
        <p class="mb-1 font-semibold text-text">Summarize what a worksheet is telling you</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">Paste a table of data and ask "what's the story here?" Claude spots trends, outliers, and the headline number — handy before you present to the team.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <CopyPrompt text="Here's a formula: [paste formula]. Explain exactly what it does, step by step, in plain English. Then tell me if there are any common edge cases or errors I should watch out for." />
  </section>

  <Callout variant="gold" title="📣 Availability & rollout">
    <p>
      The M365 Claude plugins are being rolled out at Aptera now. If you open Outlook, Word,
      PowerPoint, or Excel and don't see a Claude sidebar or add-in option yet — you're probably
      just in the queue. Reach out to <strong><a href="mailto:jake@aptera.us" class="text-gold underline underline-offset-2">jake@aptera.us</a></strong> to get bumped up or to ask about your specific app.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <TryItNow title="Try it in Outlook">
    <p>
      Find the longest unread email thread in your inbox. Open it, then open the Claude sidebar
      in Outlook. Paste the thread (or use the plugin's summarize feature) and send this prompt:
    </p>
    <CopyPrompt text="Read this email thread and give me: a one-paragraph summary of what happened, a bullet list of action items with owners (if mentioned), and any open questions that still need a decision." />
    <p>
      You should have a clean briefing in under a minute — instead of reading 40 emails.
    </p>
  </TryItNow>

  <KeyTakeaways>
    <ul>
      <li>Claude plugins live <strong>inside</strong> Outlook, Word, PowerPoint, and Excel — you don't have to leave the app you're working in.</li>
      <li>The highest-value moves: summarizing long threads, rewriting for a different audience, and explaining or generating formulas.</li>
      <li>Plugins are rolling out now — if you don't see them yet, email <a href="mailto:jake@aptera.us" class="text-gold underline underline-offset-2">jake@aptera.us</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </KeyTakeaways>
</BaseLayout>
